{"school":{"dbn":"32K045","name":"P.S./I.S. 045 Horace E. Greene","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"32","district_label":"District 32","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":445,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"84 SCHAEFER STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11207","phone":"718-821-4860","website":"https://www.psis45khoraceegreeneschool.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/71198","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"At the Horace E. Greene School, we envision that our students will develop appropriate decision making, critical thinking and technological skills that will provide them with the ability to communicate effectively. Staff and parents are focused on empowering all students with the academic skills and social experiences that will enable them to increase their educational and social goals. Students will become responsible, active, contributing members of society. All members of our community are learners who actively engage in the educational process. The school community will share accountability for creating a positive and supportive educational environment, which will result in every student achieving successful outcomes and attaining leadership qualities Instructional practices and curriculum are closely examined as a school to identify the common trends across all grades. This work helps to inform the changes that are necessary in the curriculum and/or professional development plan. The P.S./I.S. 45 student body multicultural and diverse, we celebrate our cultural diversity but we are are connected as a united PS/IS 45 Panther family. As a school, we are focusing on improving our instructional curriculum and practices to guarantee that all students learn at high levels to masterall content area standards. In addition, we utilize the I-Ready digital resource to ensure our students have opportunities to engage in personalized learning that is aligned to their diagnostic data and that provides students opportunities to accelerate their learning in ELA and Mathematics. We have a safe and inclusive school culture to support the academic and social growth of all students by instituting the following initiatives: *Kids at Hope cultural framework that reinforces our mantra that all kids are capable of success, no exceptions! *Student Council \u00c3\u00a2\u00c2\u0080\u00c2\u0093 student representatives are elected to provide student input on school issues and events. Community Service (Grades 6-8) NY Edge Afterschool Program Grades 3-8) Middle School Arts Initiative Music and the Brain (PK-2) FyreZone (Grades 2-5) Inside Broadway (Gr. 2-4) College Access (Grades 6-8) Elective Fridays (Grades 6-8) Debate Team, Gardening Team. We have re-branded our school with the addition of our mascot the P.S./I.S. 45 Panthers. We have commissioned three murals in our school which celebrates the diversity in our school community.","start_time":"08:10am","end_time":"02:29pm","languages":null,"subway":"J, Z to Chauncey St; L to Wilson Av","bus":"B20, B26, B60, B7, Q24","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Bushwick","latitude":40.686507,"longitude":-73.910206,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.87],"st":["ok"],"n":[263.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.919,0.919,0.872,0.868,0.914,0.91,0.905],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[636.0,612.0,555.0,552.0,519.0,493.0,455.0],"c":[null,null,null,null,null,0.945,0.886]},"attendance_remote_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.873],"st":["ok"],"n":[554.0]},"chronic_absent_ems_all":{"y":["2015-16","2016-17","2017-18","2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.653,0.694,0.69,0.704,0.704,0.582,0.473,0.681,0.678,0.656],"st":["ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok","ok"],"n":[754.0,731.